# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Rules are applied in order and a later, more specific rule
# overrides a header the earlier one set, which is why `/assets/*` repeats `Cache-Control`.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is deliberately absolute: the site loads nothing from anywhere else
# and asks nothing of the network at runtime (`CONSTITUTION.md` §9.1). `script-src`/`style-src`
# carry no `unsafe-inline`, so the build emits no inline `<script>` and no `style` attribute —
# Shiki's per-token colours become generated classes, and the theme is applied by `/theme.js`,
# a real file loaded synchronously. `test/site.test.ts` asserts all of that over `dist/`.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Every file under /assets/ carries a content hash in its name: fonts, the stylesheets, the module.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
